ackages/cli/\nmv _old-root-dump/tsup* ./packages/cli/\n# Configs\nmv _old-root-dump/package.json .\nmv _old-root-dump/tsconfig.json .\nmv _old-root-dump/turbo.json . 2>/dev/null || true\nmv _old-root-dump/.gitignore .root-dump/.agent .\n\n# 5. Nuke garbage forever\nrm -rf _old-root-dump\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"refactor: proper clean monorepo structure — root is sacred again\"\n\nAfter this, your repo will look like this (beautiful again):\n\ngrok-one-shot/\n├── .agent/                  # keep your magic\n├── apps/\n│   ├── site/                # Docusaurus (current live site)\n│   └── dashboard/           # ← create this next\n├── packages/\n│   ├── cli/                 # src/, tsup.config.ts, package.json\n│   ├── config/              # shared eslint, tsconfig, etc.\n│   └── ui/                  # later\n├── package.jsonig.json\n└── README.md\n\nStep 2 – Lockfile war: choose PNPM and delete the othersbash\n\nrm package-lock.json bun.lock yarn.lock 2>/dev/null\npnpm install\ngit add .\ngit commit -m \"chore: standardize on pnpm only\"\n\n3 – Add .gitignore rules so this never happens againgitignore\n\n# Temp / agent garbage\ntemp_*\ntest-*.txt\n*.backup\n*.png\n*.jpg\n*.zip\nnote-to-*.md\ntty-*.js\ndemo.js\n*.log\n\n# Only allow real code in proper folders\n!apps/\n!packages/\n!src/   # if inside packages\n\n4 – Now you can safely add the paid layer (same plan as before)Once the repo is clean (takes <2 hours), the original prompt I gave you will work perfectly with almost zero changes.Want me to:Generate the full rescue script + clean structure PR right now (15 files + git commands), or\nJust drop the final clean repo state as a zip/tar you can force-push?\n\nYou’re 2 hours away from having the cleanest, most scalable grok-one-shot repo on GitHub — and then the Pro tier will take one weekend instead of one month.Say the word and I’ll fix it in one shot. This mess is actually a good sign — it means you’ve been shipping like crazy. Now let’s professionalize it before it implodes.",
